259
00:25:13,594 --> 00:25:16,154
We ain't bad men no more.

260
00:25:16,497 --> 00:25:17,987
Shit, we're farmers.

261
00:25:18,566 --> 00:25:22,798
Should be easy killing them, supposing they don't go on down to Texas first.

262
00:25:24,805 --> 00:25:29,037
How long has it been since you fired a gun at a man, Will? Nine, ten years?

263
00:25:31,245 --> 00:25:32,371
Eleven.

264
00:25:34,315 --> 00:25:35,543
Easy, huh?

265
00:25:36,617 --> 00:25:39,677
I don't know that it was all that easy even back then.

266
00:25:39,987 --> 00:25:42,148
And we was young and full of beans.

267
00:25:43,157 --> 00:25:45,022
I mean, if you was mad at them...

268
00:25:45,793 --> 00:25:48,421
...if they'd done you wrong, I could see shooting them.

269
00:25:49,263 --> 00:25:51,731
We done stuff for money before, Ned.

270
00:25:55,603 --> 00:25:57,070
We thought we did.

271
00:25:57,772 --> 00:25:59,330
All right, so what'd these fellows do?

272
00:25:59,774 --> 00:26:04,336
Cheat at cards? Steal some strays? Spit on a rich fellow? What?

273
00:26:05,012 --> 00:26:07,003
- No, they cut up a woman. - What?

274
00:26:09,483 --> 00:26:14,216
Cut her face, cut her eyes out, cut her fingers off, cut her tits.

275
00:26:16,357 --> 00:26:18,587
Everything but her cunny, I suppose.

276
00:26:20,561 --> 00:26:22,119
I'll be dogged.

277
00:26:26,634 --> 00:26:28,431
Guess they got it coming.

278
00:26:30,037 --> 00:26:31,527
Of course, you know, Will...

279
00:26:32,973 --> 00:26:35,703
...if Claudia was alive, you wouldn't be doing this.

280
00:26:46,153 --> 00:26:48,883
I don't suppose you'd look in on my youngsters next week?

281
00:26:49,223 --> 00:26:51,555
Got some hogs they're trying to separate.

282
00:26:54,328 --> 00:26:55,955
How long are you gonna be?

283
00:26:58,732 --> 00:27:00,222
Two weeks, I guess.

284
00:27:12,246 --> 00:27:13,736
This Kid, what's he like?

285
00:27:17,117 --> 00:27:18,345
Three ways?

286
00:27:20,354 --> 00:27:23,084
I see you still have that Spencer rifle.

287
00:27:25,259 --> 00:27:28,251
And I can still knock the eye out of a bird flying, too.

288
00:27:37,872 --> 00:27:39,169
Jesus, Will.

289
00:28:36,630 --> 00:28:38,598
He must be moving right along.

290
00:28:39,099 --> 00:28:41,727
We'll come across him tomorrow, I reckon.

291
00:28:53,480 --> 00:28:57,348
Got to get used to my bed. This ain't going to be like no home.

292
00:28:59,286 --> 00:29:02,016
That ain't the only thing I'll miss, I'll tell you.

293
00:29:07,628 --> 00:29:08,925
Hell, I'm sorry.

294
00:29:09,563 --> 00:29:12,123
Don't fret it. It ain't nothing.

295
00:29:15,469 --> 00:29:17,027
She don't like it much, does she...

296
00:29:17,304 --> 00:29:18,931
...you riding off with me?

297
00:29:20,307 --> 00:29:21,934
Gave me the evil eye.

298
00:29:25,980 --> 00:29:28,210
You know, Sally's Indian and...

299
00:29:28,983 --> 00:29:31,042
...lndians ain't over-friendly.

300
00:29:33,520 --> 00:29:34,919
I don't blame her.

301
00:29:36,323 --> 00:29:38,188
I ain't gonna hold it against her.

302
00:29:38,525 --> 00:29:40,390
She knew me back then.

303
00:29:41,028 --> 00:29:42,427
She knew what a...

304
00:29:43,030 --> 00:29:45,430
...no-good son of a bitch I was.

305
00:29:47,234 --> 00:29:49,794
She ain't allowing that I changed.

306
00:29:50,671 --> 00:29:53,401
She don't realize I ain't like that no more.

307
00:29:53,674 --> 00:29:55,972
- You know women. - I ain't the same, Ned.

308
00:29:57,544 --> 00:30:02,277
Claudia, she straightened me up. Cleared me of drinking whiskey and all.

309
00:30:03,717 --> 00:30:05,275
Going on this killing...

310
00:30:05,552 --> 00:30:08,350
...don't mean I'm gonna go back to the way I was.

311
00:30:10,090 --> 00:30:11,751
I just need the money.

312
00:30:12,259 --> 00:30:14,591
Get a new start for them youngsters.

313
00:30:20,334 --> 00:30:22,632
Remember that drover I shot through the mouth...

314
00:30:22,936 --> 00:30:25,496
...and his teeth came out the back of his head?

315
00:30:28,876 --> 00:30:30,935
I think about him now and again.

316
00:30:34,114 --> 00:30:36,844
He didn't do anything to deserve to get shot.

317
00:30:37,818 --> 00:30:40,548
At least nothing I could remember when I sobered up.

318
00:30:45,926 --> 00:30:48,486
You was one crazy son of a bitch.

319
00:30:51,732 --> 00:30:53,290
No one liked me.

320
00:30:53,567 --> 00:30:57,298
The boys all thought I'd shoot them out of pure meanness.

321
00:30:59,973 --> 00:31:01,838
You ain't like that no more.

322
00:31:02,810 --> 00:31:04,971
Eagle, he hated my guts.

323
00:31:06,680 --> 00:31:09,240
Bonaparte didn't think too much of me, either.

324
00:31:09,817 --> 00:31:11,546
Quincy neither, I reckon.

325
00:31:13,987 --> 00:31:16,979
Quincy used to just watch all the time.

326
00:31:18,459 --> 00:31:19,926
Scared.

327
00:31:21,128 --> 00:31:22,595
Like I said...

328
00:31:24,131 --> 00:31:25,996
...you ain't like that no more.

329
00:31:27,000 --> 00:31:28,331
That's right.

330
00:31:29,937 --> 00:31:31,802
I'm just a fellow now.

331
00:31:32,106 --> 00:31:34,904
I ain't no different than anyone else.

332
00:31:35,676 --> 00:31:36,904
No more.

333
00:31:51,492 --> 00:31:54,052
All I want to know is what son of a bitch shot him is all.

334
00:31:54,361 --> 00:31:56,921
Was it one of them John Bulls?

335
00:31:57,364 --> 00:31:58,592
No, sir.

336
00:31:58,866 --> 00:32:03,200
The would-be assassin is a gentleman of French ancestry. Or so it would seem.

337
00:32:03,637 --> 00:32:05,935
I don't wish to give offense, when I observe...

338
00:32:06,306 --> 00:32:10,367
...the French are known to be a race of assassins...

339
00:32:10,711 --> 00:32:12,576
...who can't shoot worth a damn.

340
00:32:12,880 --> 00:32:16,543
Any Frenchmen in the present company are excluded, of course.

341
00:32:16,750 --> 00:32:20,481
Says here a fellow by the name of Guiteau. G-U-l-T...

342
00:32:21,755 --> 00:32:24,815
Sure as hell sounds like a John Bull to me.

343
00:32:25,926 --> 00:32:28,986
Well, sir, again, I don't wish to give offense...

344
00:32:29,229 --> 00:32:32,289
...when I suggest that this country should select...

345
00:32:32,566 --> 00:32:35,899
...a king or even a queen, rather than a president.

346
00:32:37,838 --> 00:32:40,705
One isn't that quick to shoot a king or a queen.

347
00:32:41,074 --> 00:32:43,634
The majesty of royalty, you see.

348
00:32:46,747 --> 00:32:49,614
Maybe you don't wish to give offense, sir...

349
00:32:50,017 --> 00:32:52,076
...but you are giving it pretty thick.

350
00:32:52,553 --> 00:32:55,283
This country don't need no queens whatsoever, I reckon.

351
00:32:55,622 --> 00:32:58,284
- When I heard about queens... - Shut up, Joe.

352
00:32:58,559 --> 00:33:01,119
What the hell's wrong with you, Thurston? This dude...

353
00:33:01,461 --> 00:33:04,294
Might be that this dude here is English Bob.

354
00:33:05,532 --> 00:33:08,330
He's the one that works for the railroad shooting Chinamen.

355
00:33:08,702 --> 00:33:11,170
Might be he's waiting for some cowboy...

356
00:33:11,438 --> 00:33:14,305
...to touch his pistol so he can shoot him down.

357
00:33:26,220 --> 00:33:27,949
Is that a fact, mister?

358
00:33:28,989 --> 00:33:30,718
You English Bob?

359
00:33:33,393 --> 00:33:34,360
Pheasants.

360
00:33:36,830 --> 00:33:38,821
Let's shoot some pheasants.

361
00:33:39,066 --> 00:33:40,294
Ten shots.

362
00:33:40,634 --> 00:33:43,296
And let's say $1 a pheasant.

363
00:33:43,971 --> 00:33:47,134
I'll shoot for the queen, and you for...

364
00:33:47,574 --> 00:33:49,132
...whomever.

365
00:34:05,626 --> 00:34:07,594
That's eight for me and one for you.

366
00:34:07,861 --> 00:34:10,421
That comes to $7.

367
00:34:11,098 --> 00:34:13,066
Pretty damn good shooting...

368
00:34:13,667 --> 00:34:15,396
...for a John Bull.

369
00:34:15,936 --> 00:34:18,666
No doubt your aim was affected by your grief...

370
00:34:21,108 --> 00:34:23,576
...over the injury to your president.

371
00:34:35,822 --> 00:34:39,883
It's the climate that does it. That, and the infernal distances.

372
00:34:40,193 --> 00:34:41,182
Does what?

373
00:34:41,662 --> 00:34:44,722
Induces people to shoot persons in high places.

374
00:34:47,134 --> 00:34:49,261
You know, it's a savage country, really.

375
00:34:49,536 --> 00:34:52,528
That's the second one they shot in 20 years.

376
00:34:53,040 --> 00:34:56,532
It's uncivilized shooting persons of substance.

377
00:35:53,700 --> 00:35:54,928
Thank you.

378
00:35:57,704 --> 00:35:59,103
Pardon me, gentlemen.

379
00:36:01,475 --> 00:36:03,966
Local ordinance obliges you to surrender all sidearms...

380
00:36:04,211 --> 00:36:07,078
...to the proper authorities for the duration of your visit.

381
00:36:07,881 --> 00:36:09,109
Proper authority?

382
00:36:12,386 --> 00:36:13,785
I can assure you, young man...

383
00:36:14,054 --> 00:36:17,615
...that neither my companion nor I carry firearms on our person.

384
00:36:18,125 --> 00:36:21,959
We rely upon the goodwill of our fellow man and the...

385
00:36:22,295 --> 00:36:24,627
...forbearance of reptiles.

386
00:36:38,378 --> 00:36:40,175
Unarmed, my ass.

387
00:36:40,881 --> 00:36:42,610
Christ, it's hot.

388
00:36:42,983 --> 00:36:47,113
If I'm going to get shot, I'd rather it was hot than cold.

389
00:36:47,754 --> 00:36:50,723
Everything hurts me more when it's cold.

390
00:36:51,024 --> 00:36:53,185
- You hit your thumb in the cold... - Shut up, Fatty!

391
00:36:54,761 --> 00:36:56,626
- I only said... - Clyde's back.

392
00:36:57,230 --> 00:36:58,891
- Is Little Bill with him? - No.

393
00:36:59,733 --> 00:37:00,791
Shit.

394
00:37:06,239 --> 00:37:08,969
- You boys clean my Remington? - Cleaned and loaded.

395
00:37:10,177 --> 00:37:12,042
Where's Little Bill, for Christ's sake?

396
00:37:12,679 --> 00:37:14,146
Building his damn porch.

397
00:37:14,915 --> 00:37:16,280
Building his porch?

398
00:37:16,917 --> 00:37:20,216
If you got shot, would you like it better on a hot or cold day?

399
00:37:20,554 --> 00:37:22,249
I ain't going to get shot.

400
00:37:24,191 --> 00:37:25,317
He's coming, ain't he?

401
00:37:26,193 --> 00:37:28,058
Of course he's coming.

402
00:37:28,962 --> 00:37:30,361
I just loaded that.

403
00:37:30,630 --> 00:37:33,622
I don't trust nobody to load my guns for a shooting.

404
00:37:35,202 --> 00:37:36,066
What'd he say?

405
00:37:36,603 --> 00:37:39,595
Bill didn't say nothing. He said he was building his porch.

406
00:37:40,474 --> 00:37:42,032
You seen that thing?

407
00:37:42,275 --> 00:37:43,833
It was all loaded.

408
00:37:44,211 --> 00:37:46,839
You got three pistols and you only got one arm!

409
00:37:47,581 --> 00:37:50,516
I just don't want to get killed for lack of shooting back.

410
00:37:53,353 --> 00:37:56,345
He don't have a straight angle on that whole damn porch!

411
00:37:56,890 --> 00:37:58,881
Or the whole house, for that matter!

412
00:37:59,226 --> 00:38:01,353
He is the worst damn carpenter.

413
00:38:02,095 --> 00:38:03,722
He didn't say nothing?

414
00:38:04,564 --> 00:38:06,429
Asked what they looked like.

415
00:38:08,134 --> 00:38:10,864
Maybe he's tough but he sure ain't no carpenter.

416
00:38:11,371 --> 00:38:13,134
Maybe he ain't so tough.

417
00:38:14,374 --> 00:38:16,035
Seem like he was scared?

418
00:38:17,978 --> 00:38:19,969
Little Bill? Him scared?

419
00:38:21,314 --> 00:38:24,477
We've never seen him up against any like these ones.

420
00:38:24,851 --> 00:38:25,715
Killers.

421
00:38:27,153 --> 00:38:30,213
Little Bill comes out of Kansas and Texas, boys.

422
00:38:31,024 --> 00:38:33,015
He worked them tough towns.

423
00:38:33,360 --> 00:38:34,657
Just wondered.

424
00:38:36,730 --> 00:38:38,561
Anybody could be scared.

425
00:38:43,670 --> 00:38:45,535
He wasn't scared, boys.

426
00:38:46,840 --> 00:38:48,569
He just ain't no carpenter.

427
00:38:54,848 --> 00:38:59,581
There's a dignity in royalty. A majesty that precludes the likelihood of assassination.

428
00:39:00,353 --> 00:39:02,753
If you were to point a pistol at a queen...

429
00:39:03,023 --> 00:39:05,514
...your hands would shake as though palsied.

430
00:39:05,825 --> 00:39:08,055
I wouldn't point no pistol at nobody.

431
00:39:09,563 --> 00:39:11,428
Always a wise policy.

432
00:39:12,332 --> 00:39:14,800
But if you did, I can assure you, if you did...

433
00:39:15,201 --> 00:39:19,604
...the sight of royalty would cause you to dismiss all thoughts of bloodshed.

434
00:39:19,873 --> 00:39:22,433
You would stand, how should I put it?

435
00:39:22,809 --> 00:39:23,833
In awe.

436
00:39:27,147 --> 00:39:28,546
Now, a president...

437
00:39:28,815 --> 00:39:31,682
Well, why not shoot the president?

438
00:39:37,924 --> 00:39:39,323
Keep the change.

439
00:39:39,593 --> 00:39:43,324
This Strawberry Alice person, tell me again.

440
00:39:43,597 --> 00:39:47,328
Down the street and across to Greely's Beer Garden and Billiards Parlor.

441
00:39:47,667 --> 00:39:50,067
Ask for Alice, say you want a game of billiards.

442
00:39:50,337 --> 00:39:51,201
Billiards?

443
00:39:51,471 --> 00:39:53,632
Even though I don't wish to play?

444
00:39:53,907 --> 00:39:57,240
No matter. They burned the table in '78 for firewood.

445
00:39:58,345 --> 00:39:59,312
Quite right.

446
00:39:59,613 --> 00:40:00,671
Quite right.

447
00:40:01,247 --> 00:40:03,875
Mr. Beauchamp, I think a cup of tea...

448
00:40:19,099 --> 00:40:20,259
Hello, Bob.

449
00:40:23,003 --> 00:40:25,403
Boys, this here is English Bob.

450
00:40:26,940 --> 00:40:28,805
Shit and fried eggs.

451
00:40:31,478 --> 00:40:32,945
Been a long time.

452
00:40:34,280 --> 00:40:35,679
Run out of Chinamen?

453
00:40:37,884 --> 00:40:40,284
I thought that you were dead.

454
00:40:41,488 --> 00:40:43,888
I see you've shaved your chin whiskers off.

455
00:40:44,924 --> 00:40:47,791
I was tasting the soup two hours after I ate it.

456
00:40:48,928 --> 00:40:50,793
Actually, what I heard was you...

457
00:40:51,031 --> 00:40:53,795
...fell off your horse. Drunk, of course.

458
00:40:54,134 --> 00:40:56,694
And that you broke your bloody neck.

459
00:40:58,238 --> 00:41:00,206
I heard that one myself, Bob.

460
00:41:00,540 --> 00:41:02,405
Hell, I even thought I was dead...

461
00:41:02,742 --> 00:41:05,302
...till I found out I was just in Nebraska.

462
00:41:06,980 --> 00:41:08,004
Who's your friend?

463
00:41:08,815 --> 00:41:10,043
W.W. Beauchamp.

464
00:41:11,317 --> 00:41:13,877
This is Little Bill Daggett.

465
00:41:14,854 --> 00:41:16,845
And friends, of course.

466
00:41:17,957 --> 00:41:20,425
From Newton, Hays? From Abilene?

467
00:41:21,461 --> 00:41:22,689
In person.

468
00:41:24,264 --> 00:41:26,562
You work for the railroads, too, Mr. Beauchamp?

469
00:41:28,668 --> 00:41:29,726
I write.

470
00:41:30,837 --> 00:41:31,826
Letters?

471
00:41:32,338 --> 00:41:34,067
Books, Bill. Books.

472
00:41:35,175 --> 00:41:36,233
Actually...

473
00:41:36,843 --> 00:41:38,708
...he's my biographer.

474
00:41:45,018 --> 00:41:47,418
I wouldn't do that if I were you.

475
00:41:55,295 --> 00:41:56,762
It's only a book.

476
00:41:57,363 --> 00:41:58,352
A book?

477
00:42:04,871 --> 00:42:06,304
That means you boys can read.

478
00:42:07,373 --> 00:42:09,603
That means you saw the signs outside of town...

479
00:42:09,876 --> 00:42:12,936
...saying surrender your firearms.

480
00:42:15,315 --> 00:42:17,180
But, like you told young Andy...

481
00:42:19,119 --> 00:42:20,711
...you're not armed, are you?

482
00:42:22,388 --> 00:42:23,946
Not really, Bill.

483
00:42:25,325 --> 00:42:28,954
Got a Peacemaker, but that wouldn't worry you, would it?

484
00:42:29,329 --> 00:42:32,787
If you don't see it. Or most particularly, if you don't hear it.

485
00:42:34,067 --> 00:42:35,728
I'm afraid so, Bob.

486
00:42:36,569 --> 00:42:38,400
I don't like firearms around.

487
00:43:00,560 --> 00:43:02,357
Be very careful with it, sonny.

488
00:43:08,768 --> 00:43:11,566
See what kind of books Mr. Beauchamp is packing here.

489
00:43:16,276 --> 00:43:18,141
Make sure you don't get wet.

490
00:43:25,185 --> 00:43:26,447
No shit.

491
00:43:26,719 --> 00:43:29,586
All he's got here is writing stuff and this here book.

492
00:43:32,826 --> 00:43:34,316
The Duck of Death?

493
00:43:34,661 --> 00:43:35,628
Duke.

494
00:43:37,797 --> 00:43:39,094
The Duke.

495
00:43:42,368 --> 00:43:44,165
Good afternoon, gentlemen.

496
00:43:44,571 --> 00:43:46,368
I'll have that.32, Bob.

497
00:43:59,919 --> 00:44:01,216
Now, Little Bill.

498
00:44:02,322 --> 00:44:05,189
You will leave me at the mercy of my enemies.

499
00:44:10,330 --> 00:44:11,490
Enemies?

500
00:44:15,001 --> 00:44:17,492
You been talking about the queen again?

501
00:44:18,738 --> 00:44:20,330
On Independence Day?

502
00:44:33,186 --> 00:44:34,915
I guess you think I'm kicking you.

503
00:44:36,656 --> 00:44:38,123
But it ain't so!

504
00:44:38,558 --> 00:44:40,389
What I'm doing is talking!

505
00:44:40,693 --> 00:44:41,557
You hear?

506
00:44:42,195 --> 00:44:44,527
Talking to all them villains down there in Kansas!

507
00:44:44,764 --> 00:44:47,255
To all those villains in Missouri!

508
00:44:55,041 --> 00:44:56,269
And all those villains...

509
00:44:57,710 --> 00:44:59,541
...down in Cheyenne!

510
00:45:05,385 --> 00:45:07,876
I'm telling them there ain't no whore's gold!

511
00:45:13,593 --> 00:45:16,585
Even if there was, they wouldn't want to come looking for it...

512
00:45:17,764 --> 00:45:18,924
...anyhow!

513
00:45:48,194 --> 00:45:49,661
What are you all looking at?

514
00:45:49,963 --> 00:45:51,157
Go on! Get out of here!

515
00:45:58,604 --> 00:46:00,469
Mind your own business!

516
00:46:29,335 --> 00:46:30,734
You ever go into town?

517
00:46:32,138 --> 00:46:33,366
On occasion.

518
00:46:33,740 --> 00:46:36,038
To sell a hog, pick up supplies.

519
00:46:37,377 --> 00:46:39,538
I mean, to get yourself a woman?

520
00:46:43,149 --> 00:46:45,276
No, I never go into town for that.

521
