It's no wonder you all emigrated to America!

777
01:07:39,266 --> 01:07:41,666
They wouldn't have you in England!

778
01:07:43,270 --> 01:07:45,067
You're a lot of savages!

779
01:07:45,339 --> 01:07:48,570
You're all a bunch of bloody savages! A curse on you!

780
01:07:51,011 --> 01:07:52,740
Nobody's going to come...

781
01:07:54,115 --> 01:07:56,845
...after what Little Bill done to that Englishman.

782
01:07:58,953 --> 01:08:01,513
Delilah, can't you get them tables clean?

783
01:08:02,389 --> 01:08:06,553
Cover your face, somebody might hump you and you wouldn't have to clean.

784
01:08:08,295 --> 01:08:10,525
What do they call those face covers?

785
01:08:10,798 --> 01:08:11,856
A veil.

786
01:08:12,099 --> 01:08:13,726
Yeah. Get a veil!

787
01:08:23,344 --> 01:08:24,811
Rain's coming.

788
01:08:25,713 --> 01:08:27,044
Thank God.

789
01:08:52,673 --> 01:08:53,731
Sure?

790
01:09:05,853 --> 01:09:07,650
You all right, Will?

791
01:09:18,265 --> 01:09:19,664
There's a fellow asking for you.

792
01:09:20,267 --> 01:09:22,258
Tonight? You ain't joshing?

793
01:09:23,370 --> 01:09:24,837
This way, mister.

794
01:09:25,372 --> 01:09:28,102
Must be randy as hell to come out in this shit.

795
01:09:38,485 --> 01:09:41,215
"No, no! You're wrong, Little Bill! " he said.

796
01:09:41,488 --> 01:09:44,651
"That's not a curly J. That's a bobbed J!"

797
01:09:45,292 --> 01:09:48,125
He had changed it over. And I said to him:

798
01:09:48,462 --> 01:09:51,454
"Jim, you're a liar and a horse thief!"

799
01:09:53,901 --> 01:09:55,960
He saw the rest of them wouldn't help him none.

800
01:09:56,203 --> 01:10:00,003
Of course he started crying and sobbing and just carrying on.

801
01:10:00,407 --> 01:10:03,638
He said, "God, please don't kill me, Bill!

802
01:10:03,978 --> 01:10:05,206
"Please don't kill me!"

803
01:10:05,479 --> 01:10:07,310
I said, "It makes me sick..."

804
01:10:08,649 --> 01:10:10,048
Open the window.

805
01:10:10,751 --> 01:10:14,050
"...to see a man carrying two pistols and a Henry rifle...

806
01:10:15,289 --> 01:10:16,916
"...and crying like a damn baby."

807
01:10:17,157 --> 01:10:18,818
So, you killed him?

808
01:10:19,059 --> 01:10:20,026
No.

809
01:10:20,594 --> 01:10:22,061
But I should have.

810
01:10:23,130 --> 01:10:24,961
I can't abide them kind.

811
01:10:25,332 --> 01:10:27,323
You see them in the taverns.

812
01:10:27,668 --> 01:10:29,898
Tramps and drunk teamsters...

813
01:10:30,337 --> 01:10:32,202
...and crazed miners.

814
01:10:33,007 --> 01:10:36,408
Sporting their pistols and acting like they was bad men.

815
01:10:36,844 --> 01:10:40,678
But without any sand or character. Not even any bad character.

816
01:10:44,485 --> 01:10:46,715
I do not like assassins.

817
01:10:48,188 --> 01:10:50,349
Or men of low character.

818
01:10:52,359 --> 01:10:53,690
Like your friend English Bob.

819
01:10:54,361 --> 01:10:56,226
But Bob was no coward, you know.

820
01:10:56,797 --> 01:10:59,766
He wouldn't go up to your face and cry and carry on like that...

821
01:11:01,335 --> 01:11:02,199
Sheriff...

822
01:11:03,637 --> 01:11:06,265
I don't have any more receptacles.

823
01:11:06,640 --> 01:11:08,608
Maybe you should just hang the carpenter.

824
01:11:10,978 --> 01:11:11,842
What?

825
01:11:14,548 --> 01:11:17,540
I was saying that because of the... If you hang...

826
01:11:19,887 --> 01:11:21,047
It doesn't matter.

827
01:11:23,357 --> 01:11:24,984
What the hell?

828
01:11:25,659 --> 01:11:27,456
On a night like this!

829
01:11:28,962 --> 01:11:30,259
Who in the hell is it?

830
01:11:30,564 --> 01:11:32,623
Deputy Charley Hecker, Bill.

831
01:11:34,601 --> 01:11:35,829
What?

832
01:11:36,503 --> 01:11:40,906
Three fellows just come into town, Bill. They're down at Greely's.

833
01:11:41,175 --> 01:11:43,040
There's two of them got guns.

834
01:11:51,452 --> 01:11:53,613
What the hell's keeping that Kid?

835
01:11:55,556 --> 01:11:57,023
You suppose he's up...

836
01:11:58,525 --> 01:12:02,086
Jesus, Will. You look like shit.

837
01:12:06,700 --> 01:12:10,932
- You remember Eagle Hendershot? - Yeah.

838
01:12:14,208 --> 01:12:15,436
I saw him.

839
01:12:17,211 --> 01:12:18,610
Will, he's dead.

840
01:12:19,546 --> 01:12:21,173
No, I saw him, Ned.

841
01:12:22,216 --> 01:12:25,447
His head was broke open. You could see inside of it.

842
01:12:27,488 --> 01:12:28,352
Jesus.

843
01:12:28,756 --> 01:12:30,155
You got a fever.

844
01:12:30,624 --> 01:12:33,457
- Take a drink, will you? - Worms were coming out.

845
01:12:38,399 --> 01:12:40,128
I'm gonna go see what's keeping the Kid.

846
01:12:40,467 --> 01:12:43,868
Must be he's getting an advance on one of the sporting ladies.

847
01:12:47,141 --> 01:12:48,631
If I was to...

848
01:12:50,577 --> 01:12:52,875
If it worked out that I could...

849
01:12:53,280 --> 01:12:56,147
...take a little time for myself, I don't suppose you would...

850
01:13:02,289 --> 01:13:04,086
I guess you wouldn't want to come.

851
01:14:26,907 --> 01:14:28,568
Give me the pistol, mister.

852
01:14:34,915 --> 01:14:36,780
I says give me over your pistol.

853
01:14:40,621 --> 01:14:41,952
I ain't drunk.

854
01:14:44,191 --> 01:14:47,820
Ordinance says you got to turn in your firearms to County Office...

855
01:14:48,695 --> 01:14:49,923
...day or night.

856
01:14:56,870 --> 01:15:00,101
I guess you didn't see the sign, with the weather and all.

857
01:15:02,209 --> 01:15:03,267
No.

858
01:15:04,711 --> 01:15:07,271
But I ain't armed.

859
01:15:09,416 --> 01:15:12,044
Your friends upstairs got any pistols?

860
01:15:17,858 --> 01:15:19,325
They ain't armed, either.

861
01:15:21,728 --> 01:15:23,127
Spilled your whiskey.

862
01:15:25,198 --> 01:15:26,495
What's your name?

863
01:15:28,569 --> 01:15:29,797
William...

864
01:15:32,639 --> 01:15:33,697
...Hendershot.

865
01:15:37,477 --> 01:15:39,877
Well, Mr. William Hendershot...

866
01:15:41,982 --> 01:15:45,315
...what if I was to say you was a no-good son of a bitch and a liar?

867
01:15:48,622 --> 01:15:52,854
And if I was to say you shit in your pants because of a cowardly soul...

868
01:15:53,961 --> 01:15:57,362
...I bet you'd show me that pistol right quick and shoot me dead.

869
01:15:57,664 --> 01:15:58,824
Isn't that so?

870
01:16:06,106 --> 01:16:07,767
Maybe, I guess.

871
01:16:09,843 --> 01:16:11,071
But the fact...

872
01:16:11,778 --> 01:16:13,006
...is I ain't...

873
01:16:13,313 --> 01:16:14,940
...carrying no firearm.

874
01:16:15,382 --> 01:16:16,440
Get up.

875
01:16:49,650 --> 01:16:51,880
What's this for, snakes and such?

876
01:16:54,354 --> 01:16:57,152
We don't have any snakes in here, Mr. Hendershot.

877
01:17:02,496 --> 01:17:03,895
It ain't loaded.

878
01:17:05,832 --> 01:17:06,696
Powder's wet.

879
01:17:10,070 --> 01:17:11,628
You see, Mr. Beauchamp?

880
01:17:14,675 --> 01:17:16,643
This is the kind of trash I'm speaking of!

881
01:17:24,885 --> 01:17:26,409
You find this kind in every saloon...

882
01:17:26,687 --> 01:17:28,814
...in all your prosperous communities!

883
01:17:29,489 --> 01:17:30,285
Wichita!

884
01:17:33,326 --> 01:17:35,191
Over in Cheyenne!

885
01:17:38,932 --> 01:17:39,990
Abilene!

886
01:17:43,704 --> 01:17:46,104
But you won't find them in the town of Big Whiskey.

887
01:17:51,411 --> 01:17:52,275
Hurry up!

888
01:17:52,546 --> 01:17:54,104
Know what to say to Little Bill?

889
01:17:54,414 --> 01:17:56,541
Look sharp for that lone pine.

890
01:17:56,883 --> 01:17:58,441
Miss the pine, you won't find it.

891
01:17:58,652 --> 01:18:00,483
Not the shirt! Put the fucking boots on!

892
01:18:10,564 --> 01:18:13,032
What are we going to do about Will?

893
01:18:13,400 --> 01:18:16,631
Come on! Let's hope them horses are still there!

894
01:18:51,104 --> 01:18:53,072
Let the man out, W.W.

895
01:18:54,107 --> 01:18:58,168
He's desiring to leave the hospitality of Big Whiskey behind him.

896
01:19:31,144 --> 01:19:34,443
Easy. She's got to work. She's got to turn $1 a time!

897
01:19:34,815 --> 01:19:37,375
How come they lit out the back window?

898
01:19:37,717 --> 01:19:40,208
On account of they seen you beating on their friend.

899
01:19:41,154 --> 01:19:43,122
They just come for the billiards, honest.

900
01:19:43,423 --> 01:19:44,287
Billiards?

901
01:19:46,393 --> 01:19:48,623
They just passing through here?

902
01:19:48,962 --> 01:19:50,395
Going to Fort Buford.

903
01:19:50,697 --> 01:19:53,564
You kicked the shit out of an innocent man.

904
01:19:54,067 --> 01:19:55,125
Innocent?

905
01:19:55,602 --> 01:19:57,001
Innocent of what?

906
01:20:15,856 --> 01:20:17,915
Jesus. Will.

907
01:20:24,097 --> 01:20:27,760
Jesus. You done this before?

908
01:20:29,469 --> 01:20:30,959
Plenty of times.

909
01:20:32,806 --> 01:20:34,637
His pistol must've jammed.

910
01:20:37,143 --> 01:20:39,202
Bring that candle in a little closer.

911
01:20:39,479 --> 01:20:40,639
I can't see.

912
01:20:52,425 --> 01:20:55,155
He wouldn't take no beating like that if it hadn't jammed.

913
01:20:56,596 --> 01:20:58,894
He wouldn't give it over and not shoot no one.

914
01:21:03,336 --> 01:21:04,997
He don't look so good.

915
01:21:07,173 --> 01:21:09,004
He didn't even pull his pistol?

916
01:21:09,309 --> 01:21:11,106
He ain't as tough as you, Kid.

917
01:21:11,378 --> 01:21:13,107
At least I'd have pulled my pistol.

918
01:21:13,380 --> 01:21:14,438
You did!

919
01:21:14,681 --> 01:21:16,512
Out of the lady and out the goddamn window!

920
01:21:16,783 --> 01:21:19,513
- That was your idea! I wanted to... - We gotta go.

921
01:21:19,853 --> 01:21:23,084
Already? Darling, I'm near ready for another advance.

922
01:21:23,390 --> 01:21:26,791
- You'll use it all up. - No more advances on what you ain't done.

923
01:21:26,993 --> 01:21:31,157
Sweetheart, we're just waiting on this weather to clear!

924
01:21:31,865 --> 01:21:33,423
We'll need more food!

925
01:21:33,967 --> 01:21:35,525
Three days' worth.

926
01:21:35,969 --> 01:21:37,527
Three days?

927
01:21:38,471 --> 01:21:41,702
- We could kill them tomorrow. - I don't kill nobody without him.

928
01:21:41,975 --> 01:21:44,535
We don't need him! The two of us could do it.

929
01:21:46,413 --> 01:21:49,075
Besides, he ain't nothing but a broken-down pig farmer.

930
01:21:49,716 --> 01:21:53,117
One of us'll bring food in the morning! We'll bring whiskey, too.

931
01:21:53,420 --> 01:21:55,479
And some medicine if you got any!

932
01:21:57,057 --> 01:21:59,287
Don't it make you sick hearing him like that?

933
01:21:59,659 --> 01:22:01,286
Don't you ladies worry none!

934
01:22:02,562 --> 01:22:05,895
Me and Ned will kill them two sons of bitches for you!

935
01:22:12,906 --> 01:22:14,305
Claudia.

936
01:22:23,083 --> 01:22:24,482
Claudia's not here.

937
01:22:24,751 --> 01:22:26,241
Is that you, Ned?

938
01:22:28,088 --> 01:22:29,419
I've seen him, Ned.

939
01:22:32,592 --> 01:22:34,753
I've seen the Angel of Death.

940
01:22:35,428 --> 01:22:37,919
I seen the river, Ned.

941
01:22:38,598 --> 01:22:40,327
He's got snake eyes.

942
01:22:40,600 --> 01:22:42,659
Who's got snake eyes?

943
01:22:43,536 --> 01:22:45,504
The Angel of Death.

944
01:22:48,942 --> 01:22:51,502
Ned, I'm scared of dying.

945
01:22:52,312 --> 01:22:53,870
Easy, partner.

946
01:22:54,614 --> 01:22:56,479
I seen Claudia, too.

947
01:22:57,417 --> 01:23:00,648
That's good you saw Claudia, ain't it?

948
01:23:01,054 --> 01:23:03,614
Her face was all covered with worms.

949
01:23:04,391 --> 01:23:05,949
Ned, I'm scared.

950
01:23:07,460 --> 01:23:08,859
I'm dying.

951
01:23:13,800 --> 01:23:15,859
No, don't tell nobody.

952
01:23:16,403 --> 01:23:18,200
Don't tell my kids...

953
01:23:18,738 --> 01:23:21,366
...none of the things I did. Hear me?

954
01:23:23,410 --> 01:23:24,638
All right.

955
01:23:42,062 --> 01:23:43,859
He's gonna die, ain't he?

956
01:23:45,331 --> 01:23:46,320
Maybe.

957
01:23:47,333 --> 01:23:49,198
Supposing he does?

958
01:23:53,106 --> 01:23:54,573
We'll bury him.

959
01:23:55,008 --> 01:23:56,873
That ain't what I mean.

960
01:24:00,380 --> 01:24:03,110
You mean, will I help you kill them cowboys?

961
01:24:05,185 --> 01:24:07,176
I can't spot them myself.

962
01:24:07,554 --> 01:24:09,044
But you could.

963
01:24:09,789 --> 01:24:13,418
That big bastard? You could spot him a half-mile off.

964
01:24:15,161 --> 01:24:16,719
And if I spot him?

965
01:24:18,164 --> 01:24:20,394
Then I ride up close and shoot him.

966
01:24:23,636 --> 01:24:24,933
Just like that?

967
01:24:25,371 --> 01:24:27,931
I'm a damn killer. I done it before.

968
01:24:31,044 --> 01:24:33,205
I'm more of a killer than he is, anyhow.

969
01:24:35,215 --> 01:24:36,079
Yeah?

970
01:24:38,785 --> 01:24:39,649
Yeah.

971
01:25:03,009 --> 01:25:04,806
I thought you was an angel.

972
01:25:06,913 --> 01:25:08,471
You ain't dead.

973
01:25:16,856 --> 01:25:18,414
Some big fellow...

974
01:25:19,592 --> 01:25:21,651
...really kicked the hell out of me.

975
01:25:24,531 --> 01:25:26,761
I must look kind of like you now.

976
01:25:28,868 --> 01:25:31,098
You don't look nothing like me, mister.

977
01:25:33,039 --> 01:25:34,666
No offense meant.

978
01:25:37,410 --> 01:25:39,878
You gotta be the one those cowboys cut up.

979
01:25:46,953 --> 01:25:49,513
My partners, Ned and that Kid...

980
01:25:50,056 --> 01:25:51,023
...they around?

981
01:25:52,559 --> 01:25:55,619
They went out scouting when they saw your fever broke.

982
01:25:56,629 --> 01:25:57,687
Scouting?

983
01:25:58,631 --> 01:26:00,496
Out to the Bar T...

984
01:26:00,900 --> 01:26:02,765
...looking for them.

985
01:26:06,906 --> 01:26:08,703
How long I been here?

986
01:26:09,909 --> 01:26:11,308
Three days.

987
01:26:12,912 --> 01:26:14,539
Are you hungry or...

988
01:26:15,281 --> 01:26:17,078
Three days?

989
01:26:17,350 --> 01:26:18,840
I ought to be.

990
01:26:31,130 --> 01:26:32,859
I thought I was gone.

991
01:26:36,002 --> 01:26:40,234
I wouldn't normally pay no notice to high country like this.

992
01:26:41,007 --> 01:26:43,498
Trees. But I'm sure noticing now.

993
01:26:44,611 --> 01:26:46,670
Thought I was dying for sure.

994
01:26:48,948 --> 01:26:50,575
I brought your hat.

995
01:26:50,850 --> 01:26:53,182
You left it down at Greely's.

996
01:26:54,187 --> 01:26:55,245
Thanks.

997
01:26:57,290 --> 01:26:58,587
That sheriff...

998
01:26:59,926 --> 01:27:01,325
...still looking for me?

999
01:27:01,628 --> 01:27:02,856
Little Bill?

1000
01:27:03,096 --> 01:27:05,656
No, he thinks you went south.

1001
01:27:08,968 --> 01:27:11,596
Are you really going to kill them cowboys?

1002
01:27:12,972 --> 01:27:14,200
I guess.

1003
01:27:15,141 --> 01:27:17,200
Still a payment coming, isn't there?

1004
01:27:19,145 --> 01:27:21,443
Them other two, your friends...

1005
01:27:22,415 --> 01:27:25,282
...they been taking advances on the payment.

1006
01:27:26,352 --> 01:27:27,751
Advances?

1007
01:27:29,756 --> 01:27:31,246
Free ones.

1008
01:27:31,391 --> 01:27:32,255
Free ones?

1009
01:27:33,726 --> 01:27:36,559
Alice and Silky been giving them free ones.

1010
01:27:38,498 --> 01:27:39,726
I see.

1011
01:27:43,503 --> 01:27:45,562
Would you like a free one?

1012
01:27:55,581 --> 01:27:56,912
I guess not.

1013
01:27:57,917 --> 01:28:01,148
I didn't mean with me. I meant...

1014
01:28:01,854 --> 01:28:04,652
...Alice and Silky would be happy to give you a free one...

1015
01:28:04,891 --> 01:28:06,449
...if you wanted one.

1016
01:28:06,893 --> 01:28:08,884
That's all I meant.

1017
01:28:13,032 --> 01:28:16,900
I didn't mean I didn't want a free one on account of you being cut up.

1018
01:28:18,037 --> 01:28:21,666
What I said the other day about you looking like me, that ain't true.

1019
01:28:22,375 --> 01:28:24,240
You ain't ugly like me.

1020
01:28:25,611 --> 01:28:28,341
It's just that we both have got scars.

1021
01:28:31,417 --> 01:28:34,875
You're a beautiful woman and if I was to want a free one...

1022
01:28:35,221 --> 01:28:38,622
...l'd want it with you, I guess, more than them other two.

1023
01:28:41,094 --> 01:28:42,425
It's just that...

1024
01:28:43,196 --> 01:28:45,494
...I can't on account of my wife.

1025
01:28:52,405 --> 01:28:53,463
Your wife?

1026
01:28:54,307 --> 01:28:56,172
Yeah. You see...

1027
01:29:02,648 --> 01:29:04,377
I admire you for that...

1028
01:29:05,151 --> 01:29:06,641
...for being true to your wife.

1029
01:29:08,621 --> 01:29:10,589
I've known a lot of men...

1030
01:29:12,959 --> 01:29:14,290
...who weren't.

1031
01:29:16,763 --> 01:29:18,230
I suppose.

1032
01:29:24,771 --> 01:29:26,500
Is she back in Kansas?

1033
01:29:30,676 --> 01:29:33,236
She's watching over my young ones.

1034
01:29:38,484 --> 01:29:39,610
Hang on!

1035
01:29:39,852 --> 01:29:41,717
Get the damn iron!

1036
01:29:51,431 --> 01:29:52,830
Jesus, fella.

1037
01:30:05,044 --> 01:30:07,444
Jesus, boys, my leg's broke!

1038
01:30:09,415 --> 01:30:11,280
I'm pinned, boys!

1039
01:30:12,418 --> 01:30:13,976
Better finish him.

1040
01:30:14,587 --> 01:30:16,817
He ain't dead? You didn't get him?

1041
01:30:17,056 --> 01:30:18,614
He got the boy's horse.

1042
01:30:19,559 --> 01:30:21,891
Better finish him before he gets clear.

1043
01:30:24,730 --> 01:30:26,561
Get behind them rocks.

1044
01:30:27,033 --> 01:30:28,591
Get over there!

1045
01:30:31,904 --> 01:30:34,634
What happened? He ain't killed?

1046
01:30:35,174 --> 01:30:36,141
What's going on?

1047
01:30:36,509 --> 01:30:38,977
He gets in those rocks, we ain't gonna get him.

1048
01:30:39,378 --> 01:30:41,846
- Unless we go down there. - What rocks?

1049
01:30:42,181 --> 01:30:44,979
Why don't you shoot? What's going on?

1050
01:30:49,856 --> 01:30:50,982
Ain't you gonna shoot?

1051
01:31:04,604 --> 01:31:06,765
I ain't very good with one of these.

1052
01:31:12,612 --> 01:31:15,012
Keep going, Davey! The rocks!

1053
01:31:17,316 --> 01:31:18,374
Get him?

1054
01:31:19,418 --> 01:31:20,646
Where is he?

1055
01:31:20,953 --> 01:31:23,114
How many more shots do I have?

1056
01:31:25,091 --> 01:31:27,924
Ned, goddamn it, how many more shots do I have?

1057
01:31:31,097 --> 01:31:32,086
Two.

1058
01:31:42,341 --> 01:31:43,569
Go, Davey!

1059
01:31:44,410 --> 01:31:45,707
Did you get him?

1060
01:32:03,129 --> 01:32:04,994
Here, reload this.

1061
01:32:06,265 --> 01:32:08,563
- You missed him. - I got him.

1062
01:32:12,605 --> 01:32:13,902
He ain't killed.

1063
01:32:14,607 --> 01:32:16,336
Maybe, maybe not.

1064
01:32:17,009 --> 01:32:19,068
Got him through the gut, I think.

1065
01:32:23,616 --> 01:32:25,243
You think he's gonna die?

1066
01:32:27,687 --> 01:32:28,915
You think we killed him?

1067
01:32:32,024 --> 01:32:34,254
He shot me.

1068
01:32:39,699 --> 01:32:40,927
We killed him...

1069
01:32:41,367 --> 01:32:42,595
...I guess.

1070
01:32:46,639 --> 01:32:48,504
I'm dying, boys!

1071
01:32:49,208 --> 01:32:52,769
Then you shouldn't have cut up no woman, you asshole!

1072
01:32:58,584 --> 01:33:00,745
Jesus, I'm so thirsty.

1073
01:33:05,191 --> 01:33:07,182
Give me some water, please!

1074
01:33:07,660 --> 01:33:08,888
Please, Slim!

1075
01:33:10,129 --> 01:33:11,756
I'm bleeding, Slim!

1076
01:33:16,068 --> 01:33:18,730
Give him a drink of water, goddamn it!

1077
01:33:20,006 --> 01:33:22,736
Give me a drink of water, would you, Slim?

1078
01:33:22,908 --> 01:33:26,901
Will you give him a drink of water, for Christ's sake? We ain't gonna shoot!

1079
01:33:29,015 --> 01:33:31,142
- You ain't gonna shoot? - No.

1080
01:33:34,453 --> 01:33:36,114
Hold on, Davey-boy!

1081
01:33:37,356 --> 01:33:38,823
Here I come now!

1082
01:33:45,364 --> 01:33:47,229
Don't you shoot me, you bastards!

1083
01:33:50,936 --> 01:33:52,164
Shit!

1084
01:34:02,114 --> 01:34:04,844
- They take him water? - Yeah.

1085
01:34:06,485 --> 01:34:08,715
Jesus, Johnny! They shot him!

1086
01:34:08,954 --> 01:34:10,512
Hold on now!

1087
01:34:19,298 --> 01:34:22,790
You murdering bastards! You killed our Davey-boy!

1088
01:34:31,744 --> 01:34:33,541
When are we gonna double back?

1089
01:34:34,346 --> 01:34:36,075
After a ways.

1090
01:34:37,450 --> 01:34:38,576
Not me.

1091
01:34:39,518 --> 01:34:41,679
I'm heading on back down to Kansas.

1092
01:34:41,921 --> 01:34:43,980
We gotta kill the other one first.

1093
01:34:44,957 --> 01:34:49,189
With any luck, we'll find him by nightfall or in the morning.

1094
01:34:49,495 --> 01:34:52,055
Then we can shoot him and head on back with the money.

1095
01:34:54,333 --> 01:34:55,823
Want the Spencer?

1096
01:34:56,102 --> 01:34:57,831
This ain't no time to quit.

1097
01:34:58,104 --> 01:35:00,163
- You'll lose your share, Ned. - Shut up!

1098
01:35:00,506 --> 01:35:03,168
I'll see you, Will. So long, Kid.

1099
01:35:12,618 --> 01:35:15,178
I ain't no good with that damn thing, anyhow.

1100
01:35:15,788 --> 01:35:20,521
Me and the Kid'll go over to that ranch and, when we find him, we'll shoot him.

1101
01:35:20,926 --> 01:35:24,555
We'll meet up with you, pick up our money, and all head south together.

1102
01:35:25,464 --> 01:35:27,762
Suppose he don't go back to the ranch?

1103
01:35:28,300 --> 01:35:32,168
He ain't going into town. He won't stay out in the open country.

1104
01:35:32,471 --> 01:35:34,701
He'll hole up at that ranch.

1105
01:35:36,475 --> 01:35:37,942
I ain't waiting.

1106
01:35:38,477 --> 01:35:41,037
I'll look in on your young ones.

1107
01:35:47,820 --> 01:35:50,618
Don't pay no attention to what the Kid said about the money.

1108
01:35:50,890 --> 01:35:52,118
I'll bring your share.

1109
01:35:56,395 --> 01:35:57,953
Kid's full of shit.

1110
01:36:26,192 --> 01:36:28,353
Just doing some repairs up here.

1111
01:36:28,727 --> 01:36:30,558
They killed one of them cowboys.

1112
01:36:34,667 --> 01:36:35,895
Shit.

1113
01:36:37,403 --> 01:36:41,806
Parsons said he saw three men, right after sun-up, headed out east.

1114
01:36:42,408 --> 01:36:46,469
One was on a dun and another was on a flea-bitten gray.

1115
01:36:46,745 --> 01:36:50,112
He didn't know what the third one was on, could've been an appaloosa...

1116
01:36:50,316 --> 01:36:52,045
...because he was looking into the sun.

1117
01:36:52,184 --> 01:36:56,052
Amos says to ask if the county's going to pay for feed for all the horses or not.

1118
01:36:56,288 --> 01:36:59,621
Witherspoon says he won't sell us no more.30-30 shells without we pay.

1119
01:36:59,825 --> 01:37:01,224
Hell, use my dogs.

1120
01:37:01,527 --> 01:37:03,825
Then the county's gotta take responsibility.

1121
01:37:04,697 --> 01:37:09,100
Don't worry. You get out there to the Bar T and make sure that other cowboy...

1122
01:37:09,435 --> 01:37:11,995
...stays put and don't expose himself, you hear?

1123
01:37:22,047 --> 01:37:24,345
I didn't think they'd really do it.

1124
01:37:24,884 --> 01:37:27,751
Think they come clear up from Kansas to fuck us?

1125
01:37:31,390 --> 01:37:34,257
But that Kid, he's just a boy. And the other one...

1126
01:37:34,860 --> 01:37:37,727
...Will, the nice one, being so true to his wife...

1127
01:37:38,097 --> 01:37:40,497
Wife? He ain't got no wife.

1128
01:37:41,066 --> 01:37:43,933
- Yes, he does. He said... - He ain't got no wife.

1129
01:37:44,403 --> 01:37:46,268
Not above ground, anyways.

1130
01:37:52,411 --> 01:37:53,810
Murdering whores!

1131
01:37:54,980 --> 01:37:56,470
He had it coming...

1132
01:37:56,815 --> 01:37:58,373
...for what he done.

1133
01:37:58,751 --> 01:38:00,048
And the other one, too!

1134
01:38:00,352 --> 01:38:02,582
Both of them for what they done!

1135
01:38:12,765 --> 01:38:14,164
We got one!

1136
01:38:16,602 --> 01:38:19,230
We got one, Sheriff! Out by Cow Creek!

1137
01:38:19,505 --> 01:38:20,733
Is he alive?

1138
01:38:21,006 --> 01:38:24,407
Yeah! Bunch of us boys from Bar T went out looking...

1139
01:38:24,677 --> 01:38:26,838
...on account of them killed one of our own.

1140
01:38:27,179 --> 01:38:30,342
Come across this son of a bitch on a roan heading south.

1141
01:38:30,683 --> 01:38:31,911
He admit it?

1142
01:38:32,318 --> 01:38:36,379
No. But I guess he will soon enough. Had a Spencer rifle on him.

1143
01:38:37,122 --> 01:38:38,589
Those cowboys messing him up?

1144
01:38:40,159 --> 01:38:41,649
A little bit, I guess.

1145
01:38:45,364 --> 01:38:49,357
Get out there. See if you can find out what happened to those other two fellows!

1146
01:39:12,324 --> 01:39:14,554
See anything out there, Buck?

1147
01:39:14,960 --> 01:39:18,691
Hell, yes! Seen about 200 fellows packing rifles.

1148
01:39:19,131 --> 01:39:22,589
Got the place surrounded. Say they want Quick Mike's ass.

1149
01:39:23,502 --> 01:39:26,801
I said, "How much?" They says, "About five." I said, "Dollars?"

1150
01:39:27,072 --> 01:39:28,300
They said, "Cents."

1151
01:39:28,574 --> 01:39:30,064
I said, "Sold."

1152
01:39:31,744 --> 01:39:33,405
Well, I ain't worried!

1153
01:39:33,746 --> 01:39:35,976
'Cause I got me some protection.

1154
01:40:01,774 --> 01:40:03,639
- Tell you where them others is? - Nope.

1155
01:40:03,942 --> 01:40:05,000
Given any names?

1156
01:40:05,411 --> 01:40:08,039
Didn't tell us nothing but his own name, Ned Roundtree.

1157
01:40:10,616 --> 01:40:11,844
Bring him in.

1158
01:40:14,887 --> 01:40:17,685
You'll want to tell me and Mr. Beauchamp here...

1159
01:40:18,457 --> 01:40:20,687
...all about your two villainous friends.

1160
01:40:21,393 --> 01:40:25,454
I'll want the names and whereabouts of those murderous sons of bitches.

1161
01:40:40,345 --> 01:40:42,006
Sure is ripe.

1162
01:40:43,649 --> 01:40:45,480
Going to get a lot riper.

1163
01:40:46,919 --> 01:40:48,477
Think he's still in there?

1164
01:40:50,089 --> 01:40:51,317
He's in there.

1165
01:40:52,591 --> 01:40:55,651
He's holding on to his shit like it was money.

1166
01:40:56,595 --> 01:40:57,994
He's in there.

1167
01:40:58,497 --> 01:41:00,658
Tell me right off if you see him.

1168
01:41:03,102 --> 01:41:05,161
You ain't gonna shoot him yourself, are you?

1169
01:41:05,671 --> 01:41:07,161
You can shoot him.

1170
01:41:46,645 --> 01:41:49,876
You, Mr. Quincy and... What was the young fellow's name?

1171
01:41:54,520 --> 01:41:55,919
Elroy Tate.

1172
01:42:00,859 --> 01:42:03,259
No, that's not what you said.

1173
01:42:03,729 --> 01:42:04,787
Hell if it ain't.

1174
01:42:05,130 --> 01:42:06,688
No, you said:

1175
01:42:07,332 --> 01:42:10,062
"Elroy Quincy out of Medicine Hat and...

1176
01:42:11,837 --> 01:42:13,702
"...Henry Tate out of Cheyenne."

1177
01:42:15,073 --> 01:42:16,472
Hell if I did.

1178
01:42:17,509 --> 01:42:18,908
Hell if I did.

1179
01:42:21,180 --> 01:42:24,411
Go get them whores that fucked these boys the night of the storm.

1180
01:42:24,683 --> 01:42:26,742
Strawberry Alice and Silky?

1181
01:42:27,085 --> 01:42:28,746
Go on and get them!

1182
01:42:37,930 --> 01:42:41,093
Them whores will tell different lies than you.

1183
01:42:43,268 --> 01:42:46,260
And when their lies ain't the same as your lies...

1184
01:42:48,774 --> 01:42:50,639
I ain't gonna hurt no woman.

1185
01:42:52,044 --> 01:42:53,841
But I'm gonna hurt you.

1186
01:42:56,548 --> 01:42:58,413
Not gentle like before...

1187
01:43:00,118 --> 01:43:01,608
...but bad.

1188
01:43:18,437 --> 01:43:19,495
Where you going?

1189
01:43:19,805 --> 01:43:22,296
- Out to the shithouse. - Let me finish this hand.

1190
01:43:22,574 --> 01:43:24,542
You gonna protect me while I take a dump?

1191
01:43:24,810 --> 01:43:26,971
- You'll get bushwhacked. - I'll fart on them.

1192
01:43:27,346 --> 01:43:30,338
- I'll go with him. - You can wipe my ass, Thirsty.

1193
01:43:30,649 --> 01:43:33,880
Hell with him. The man ain't polite, he ought to get shot.

1194
01:43:37,956 --> 01:43:38,945
Is that him?

1195
01:43:39,591 --> 01:43:41,058
Yeah, that's him.

1196
01:43:44,963 --> 01:43:47,295
Go get him. He's all yours.

1197
01:44:24,369 --> 01:44:25,427
Assassins!

1198
01:44:29,341 --> 01:44:30,103
Shoot them!

1199
01:44:46,491 --> 01:44:48,049
Come on, goddamn it!

1200
01:45:05,277 --> 01:45:07,336
- Get him? - Yeah.

1201
01:45:19,524 --> 01:45:20,388
Cover me.

1202
01:45:23,061 --> 01:45:25,052
- I can't see them! - Just shoot!

1203
01:45:35,540 --> 01:45:36,939
Get him!

1204
01:46:02,567 --> 01:46:04,865
Was that what it was like in the old days?

1205
01:46:05,804 --> 01:46:07,863
Everybody riding out, shooting...

1206
01:46:08,807 --> 01:46:12,641
...smoke all over the place, folks yelling, bullets whizzing by?

1207
01:46:14,579 --> 01:46:15,876
I guess so.

1208
01:46:19,985 --> 01:46:22,476
Shit, I thought they was gonna get us.

1209
01:46:23,688 --> 01:46:25,679
I was even scared a little.

1210
01:46:25,957 --> 01:46:27,185
Just for a minute.

1211
01:46:29,961 --> 01:46:31,952
Was you ever scared in them days?

1212
01:46:34,266 --> 01:46:35,665
I can't remember.

1213
01:46:37,002 --> 01:46:39,163
I was drunk most of the time.

1214
01:46:46,011 --> 01:46:48,502
I shot that fucker three times!

1215
01:46:50,182 --> 01:46:53,015
Taking a shit, he went for his pistol, and I blazed away.

1216
01:46:54,019 --> 01:46:55,247
First shot...

1217
01:46:57,289 --> 01:46:58,916
...I got him right in the chest.

1218
01:47:03,061 --> 01:47:05,120
- Say, Will. - Yeah?

1219
01:47:08,700 --> 01:47:10,099
That was the first one.

1220
01:47:11,703 --> 01:47:12,931
First one what?

1221
01:47:15,474 --> 01:47:17,271
First one I ever killed.

1222
01:47:21,346 --> 01:47:23,746
You know how I said I shot five men?

1223
01:47:25,150 --> 01:47:26,708
It weren't true.

1224
01:47:29,154 --> 01:47:31,281
That Mexican who come at me with a knife...

1225
01:47:32,557 --> 01:47:34,548
...I just busted his leg with a shovel.

1226
01:47:34,860 --> 01:47:36,725
I didn't kill him or nothing.

1227
01:47:40,332 --> 01:47:43,199
You sure killed the hell out of that fellow today.

1228
01:47:45,570 --> 01:47:46,798
Hell, yeah!

1229
01:47:50,509 --> 01:47:52,568
I killed the hell out of him, didn't I?

1230
01:47:53,745 --> 01:47:56,305
Three shots while he was taking a shit...

1231
01:48:03,388 --> 01:48:04,685
Take a drink.

1232
01:48:29,881 --> 01:48:31,439
It don't seem real.

1233
01:48:33,418 --> 01:48:35,978
How he ain't gonna never breathe again, ever.

1234
01:48:37,455 --> 01:48:38,786
How he's dead.

1235
01:48:40,625 --> 01:48:42,115
And the other one, too.

1236
01:48:45,030 --> 01:48:47,157
All on account of pulling a trigger.

1237
01:48:50,201 --> 01:48:52,431
It's a hell of a thing, killing a man.

1238
01:48:54,739 --> 01:48:56,536
You take away all he's got...

1239
01:48:57,742 --> 01:48:59,607
...and all he's ever gonna have.

1240
01:49:05,450 --> 01:49:07,179
I guess they had it coming.

1241
01:49:13,425 --> 01:49:15,290
We all have it coming, Kid.

1242
01:49:30,308 --> 01:49:33,175
I was watching you. Seeing you weren't followed.

1243
01:49:34,613 --> 01:49:38,481
Silky and Faith rode off to the east and two deputies is following them.

1244
01:49:45,523 --> 01:49:47,514
Want to help me count this stuff, Kid?

1245
01:49:47,792 --> 01:49:51,023
- I trust you. - Don't go trusting me too much.

1246
01:49:52,631 --> 01:49:55,862
In fact, we'll give Ned his share together.

1247
01:49:56,101 --> 01:49:58,501
That way you'll know I ain't holding out on you.

1248
01:49:58,970 --> 01:50:00,267
Ned's share?

1249
01:50:03,375 --> 01:50:05,434
He went south. We'll catch up to him.

1250
01:50:06,144 --> 01:50:07,702
He's dead.

1251
01:50:11,349 --> 01:50:12,816
What do you mean he's dead?

1252
01:50:14,152 --> 01:50:16,780
He went south yesterday. He ain't dead.

1253
01:50:17,489 --> 01:50:20,049
They killed him. I thought you knew that.

1254
01:50:20,325 --> 01:50:22,190
Nobody killed Ned!

1255
01:50:22,494 --> 01:50:24,962
He didn't kill anyone, he went south!

1256
01:50:25,196 --> 01:50:27,187
Why would anybody kill Ned?

1257
01:50:30,101 --> 01:50:31,261
Who killed him?

1258
01:50:32,070 --> 01:50:33,298
Little Bill.

1259
01:50:33,672 --> 01:50:36,140
The Bar T boys caught him. Little Bill...

1260
01:50:37,208 --> 01:50:38,436
...beat him up.

1261
01:50:38,710 --> 01:50:43,272
He was making him answer questions and beating him up. Then Ned just died.

1262
01:50:44,015 --> 01:50:46,643
They got a sign on him, says he was a killer.

1263
01:50:46,918 --> 01:50:48,146
They got a sign on him?

1264
01:50:48,920 --> 01:50:50,478
In front of Greely's.

1265
01:50:50,722 --> 01:50:52,883
A sign on him in front of Greely's!

1266
01:50:57,529 --> 01:50:59,827
These questions Little Bill was asking...

1267
01:51:01,066 --> 01:51:02,294
...what kind were they?

1268
01:51:07,072 --> 01:51:09,370
About where you and him was.

1269
01:51:09,774 --> 01:51:11,002
Then what?

1270
01:51:12,110 --> 01:51:16,444
A cowboy come in saying you killed Quick Mike in the shithouse at the Bar T.

1271
01:51:17,549 --> 01:51:20,416
So, Little Bill killed him for what we done?

1272
01:51:20,785 --> 01:51:22,343
Not on purpose.

1273
01:51:22,887 --> 01:51:24,855
But he started hurting him worse.

1274
01:51:25,090 --> 01:51:26,819
Making him tell stuff.

1275
01:51:27,192 --> 01:51:28,591
First, Ned wouldn't say nothing.

1276
01:51:29,561 --> 01:51:33,292
Then Little Bill hurt him so bad, he said who you was.

1277
01:51:35,400 --> 01:51:38,801
He said how you was really William Munny out of Missouri.

1278
01:51:39,637 --> 01:51:41,867
Little Bill said, "The same William Munny...

1279
01:51:42,040 --> 01:51:46,101
"...who dynamited the Rock Island and Pacific in '69, killing women and children?"

1280
01:51:46,644 --> 01:51:49,477
Ned said you done a lot worse than that. Said you was...

1281
01:51:49,647 --> 01:51:51,979
...more cold-blooded than William Bonney.

1282
01:51:52,283 --> 01:51:55,514
And how if he hurt Ned again, you was gonna come kill him...

1283
01:51:55,754 --> 01:51:58,484
...like you killed the U.S. Marshal in '70.

1284
01:52:03,595 --> 01:52:05,722
That didn't scare Little Bill, did it?

1285
01:52:07,766 --> 01:52:08,994
No, sir.

1286
01:52:17,008 --> 01:52:18,566
Give me your Schofield.

1287
01:52:19,177 --> 01:52:20,337
What for?

1288
01:52:20,612 --> 01:52:23,843
- Give it to me. - Sure.

1289
01:52:29,020 --> 01:52:30,419
You keep it.

1290
01:52:31,089 --> 01:52:32,386
I'm never gonna use it again.

1291
01:52:34,993 --> 01:52:36,984
I won't kill nobody no more.

1292
01:52:40,698 --> 01:52:42,256
I ain't like you, Will.

1293
01:52:46,371 --> 01:52:48,236
You better ride on back, miss.

1294
01:52:53,044 --> 01:52:55,376
Keep all of it. It's yours.

1295
01:52:56,514 --> 01:52:59,745
What about the spectacles and fancy clothes?

1296
01:53:00,652 --> 01:53:03,280
I guess I'd rather be blind and ragged than dead.

1297
01:53:04,789 --> 01:53:06,586
You don't have to worry, Kid.

1298
01:53:06,858 --> 01:53:08,587
I ain't going to kill you.

1299
01:53:09,327 --> 01:53:11,386
You're the only friend I got.

1300
01:53:19,337 --> 01:53:21,703
Take this money and give my half...

1301
01:53:22,073 --> 01:53:23,802
...and Ned's half to my kids.

1302
01:53:24,409 --> 01:53:27,970
Tell them if I ain't back in a week, to give half to Sally Two Trees.

1303
01:53:28,279 --> 01:53:30,941
You keep the rest. Get them spectacles.

1304
01:53:31,216 --> 01:53:32,945
You're gonna kill Little Bill, ain't you?

1305
01:53:33,451 --> 01:53:35,681
You stay clear of folks you see.

1306
01:53:35,920 --> 01:53:37,478
Be a lot of them out to hang you.

1307
01:53:37,889 --> 01:53:39,117
Get going.

1308
01:54:23,067 --> 01:54:26,935
I'm gonna say this just one more time, so don't ask me again!

1309
01:54:27,605 --> 01:54:31,905
Those on the posse today got one drink coming from the county budget!

1310
01:54:34,178 --> 01:54:37,341
And those who rode yesterday get one drink for that, too.

1311
01:54:39,117 --> 01:54:40,175
Hold it!

1312
01:54:40,785 --> 01:54:42,082
That's two!

1313
01:54:42,487 --> 01:54:45,285
After that, it comes out of your own pocket! Hear me, Skinny?

1314
01:54:45,623 --> 01:54:48,183
We'll pull out early in the morning.

1315
01:54:48,660 --> 01:54:52,892
We'll chase these fellows clear to Texas, so don't spend too much money.

1316
01:54:53,998 --> 01:54:56,489
We're gonna divide up into four parties!

1317
01:54:56,834 --> 01:54:59,234
We'll hit all the farms and trails...

1318
01:54:59,504 --> 01:55:00,903
...to make a big circle.

1319
01:55:01,272 --> 01:55:03,069
We're bound to come across somebody...

1320
01:55:03,341 --> 01:55:05,400
...who's seen these skunks.

1321
01:55:22,860 --> 01:55:25,021
Who's the fellow who owns this shithole?

1322
01:55:34,639 --> 01:55:35,936
You, fat man.

1323
01:55:36,474 --> 01:55:37,702
Speak up.

1324
01:55:40,411 --> 01:55:42,276
I own this establishment.

1325
01:55:45,817 --> 01:55:49,048
I bought it from Greely for $1,000.

1326
01:55:50,822 --> 01:55:52,289
You better clear out of there.

1327
01:55:55,326 --> 01:55:56,725
Just hold it right there!

1328
01:56:07,572 --> 01:56:10,234
Sir, you are a cowardly son of a bitch!

1329
01:56:11,843 --> 01:56:13,470
You just shot an unarmed man.

1330
01:56:14,178 --> 01:56:18,911
He should've armed himself if he's gonna decorate his saloon with my friend.

1331
01:56:19,851 --> 01:56:22,319
You'd be William Munny out of Missouri...

1332
01:56:22,920 --> 01:56:24,751
...killer of women and children.

1333
01:56:25,423 --> 01:56:26,651
That's right.

1334
01:56:28,760 --> 01:56:30,489
I've killed women and children.

1335
01:56:32,263 --> 01:56:35,926
I killed just about everything that walked or crawled at one time or another.

1336
01:56:37,368 --> 01:56:39,666
And I'm here to kill you, Little Bill.

1337
01:56:40,872 --> 01:56:42,601
For what you did to Ned.

1338
01:56:47,412 --> 01:56:49,141
You boys better move away.

1339
01:56:59,557 --> 01:57:00,854
Gentlemen...

1340
01:57:01,559 --> 01:57:03,686
...he's got one barrel left.

1341
01:57:04,729 --> 01:57:06,959
When he fires that, take out your pistols...

1342
01:57:07,198 --> 01:57:10,065
...and shoot him down like the mangy scoundrel he is!

1343
01:57:24,582 --> 01:57:27,050
Misfire! Kill the son of a bitch!

1344
01:58:03,654 --> 01:58:07,715
Any man don't want to get killed, better clear on out the back.

1345
01:58:52,303 --> 01:58:54,100
I'm shot! I've been shot!

1346
01:58:54,572 --> 01:58:55,971
You ain't shot.

1347
01:59:02,079 --> 01:59:04,741
I don't have a gun. I am not armed.

1348
01:59:06,617 --> 01:59:07,948
Pick up that rifle.

1349
01:59:10,087 --> 01:59:11,145
Pick it up.

1350
01:59:13,524 --> 01:59:14,582
Shells, too.

1351
01:59:27,872 --> 01:59:29,271
You killed Little Bill.

1352
01:59:30,841 --> 01:59:32,308
Sure you ain't armed?

1353
01:59:34,779 --> 01:59:36,644
I'm not. I don't have a gun.

1354
01:59:36,948 --> 01:59:39,610
I've never had a gun. I write. I'm a writer!

1355
01:59:41,118 --> 01:59:42,278
A writer?

1356
01:59:43,421 --> 01:59:45,548
- Letters and such? - Books.

1357
01:59:46,190 --> 01:59:47,248
Books.

1358
01:59:47,925 --> 01:59:51,793
I don't believe it, you killed five men. Single-handed.

1359
02:00:00,471 --> 02:00:02,632
That's a Spencer rifle, right?

1360
02:00:11,582 --> 02:00:12,981
Who'd you kill first?

1361
02:00:16,921 --> 02:00:19,151
"When confronted by superior numbers...

1362
02:00:19,423 --> 02:00:22,551
"...an experienced gunfighter will fire on the best shot first."

1363
02:00:23,661 --> 02:00:26,528
Little Bill told me that. You probably killed him first.

1364
02:00:28,132 --> 02:00:30,123
I was lucky in the order.

1365
02:00:31,135 --> 02:00:33,968
I've always been lucky when it comes to killing folks.

1366
02:00:37,775 --> 02:00:39,834
Who was next? Clyde, right?

1367
02:00:40,111 --> 02:00:42,739
You must have killed Clyde, or maybe Deputy Andy...

1368
02:00:43,114 --> 02:00:45,582
All I can tell you is who's gonna be last.

1369
02:01:22,219 --> 02:01:24,084
I don't deserve this...

1370
02:01:26,324 --> 02:01:27,882
...to die like this.

1371
02:01:30,961 --> 02:01:32,690
I was building a house.

1372
02:01:33,731 --> 02:01:36,291
"Deserve" has got nothing to do with it.

1373
02:01:39,070 --> 02:01:41,300
I'll see you in hell, William Munny.

1374
02:02:21,779 --> 02:02:23,940
All right, I'm coming out!

1375
02:02:24,415 --> 02:02:27,043
Any man I see out there, I'm gonna kill him!

1376
02:02:27,785 --> 02:02:30,117
Any son of a bitch takes a shot at me...

1377
02:02:31,088 --> 02:02:33,750
...l'm not only gonna kill him, but his wife...

1378
02:02:34,024 --> 02:02:35,753
...and all his friends...

1379
02:02:36,293 --> 02:02:38,523
...and burn his damn house down!

1380
02:02:45,736 --> 02:02:47,533
Nobody better shoot!

1381
02:03:03,087 --> 02:03:05,146
Charley, go ahead. Shoot him!

1382
02:03:21,105 --> 02:03:23,073
Hell, no! I ain't no deputy!

1383
02:03:43,794 --> 02:03:46,092
You better bury Ned right!

1384
02:03:46,997 --> 02:03:50,228
You better not cut up nor otherwise harm no whores!

1385
02:03:54,638 --> 02:03:58,039
Or I'll come back and kill every one of you sons of bitches.

